24.0, 22.8 "},{"bbox":{"b":411.4525489807129,"coord_origin":"TOPLEFT","l":376.28039288520813,"r":509.95163547992706,"t":400.0858474969864},"col_span":1,"column_header":false,"end_col_offset_idx":6,"end_row_offset_idx":5,"fillable":false,"row_header":false,"row_section":false,"row_span":1,"start_col_offset_idx":5,"start_row_offset_idx":4,"text":"(0.53, 0.46), (0.51, 0.46), (0.51, 0.45) "}]},"footnotes":[{"$ref":"#/texts/3"}],"label":"table","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":425.837646484375,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":69.43069458007812,"r":530.0487670898438,"t":532.6520385742188},"charspan":[0,0],"page_no":1}],"references":[],"self_ref":"#/tables/0"}],"texts":[{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Submitted to","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":771.1439829101563,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":333.67,"r":398.4100000000001,"t":781.4759829101563},"charspan":[0,12],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/0","text":"Submitted to"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"56.5 lm W  1 and 26.3%, respectively, with CRI of 86. Even at 10000 and 15000 cd m  2 , high PEs (45.8 and 38.5 lm W  1 ) and EQEs (24.3 and 22.1%) are maintained. Lighting sources are generally characterized by their total  emitted light,  which  is  a  factor  of  1.7-2.3  times  more than the forward viewing efficiencies. [1a] Therefore, the present device should have total PE and EQE values approaching 100 lm W -1 and 50%, respectively, at 5000 cd m -2 ,  which are also  the  highest  levels  reported  for  WOLEDs  with  extra  out-coupling  and/or  multi-layer tandem structures, [14] as well as comparable to the most efficient lighting technologies. [15]","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":588.2139829101563,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":70.824,"r":527.5,"t":769.4917029101563},"charspan":[0,670],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/1","text":"56.5 lm W  1 and 26.3%, respectively, with CRI of 86. Even at 10000 and 15000 cd m  2 , high PEs (45.8 and 38.5 lm W  1 ) and EQEs (24.3 and 22.1%) are maintained. Lighting sources are generally characterized by their total  emitted light,  which  is  a  factor  of  1.7-2.3  times  more than the forward viewing efficiencies. [1a] Therefore, the present device should have total PE and EQE values approaching 100 lm W -1 and 50%, respectively, at 5000 cd m -2 ,  which are also  the  highest  levels  reported  for  WOLEDs  with  extra  out-coupling  and/or  multi-layer tandem structures, [14] as well as comparable to the most efficient lighting technologies. [15]"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Table 1. Summary of EL performance for Devices 1, 2, 3 and 4.","parent":{"$ref":"#/tables/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":533.0139829101563,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":70.824,"r":380.11,"t":543.3459829101563},"charspan":[0,61],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"Table 1. Summary of EL performance for Devices 1, 2, 3 and 4."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"footnote","orig":"a) Applied voltage required to reach a luminance of 1 cd m -2 . b) Values at 1000, 5000 and 10000 cd m -2 , respectively.","parent":{"$ref":"#/tables/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":398.9539829101563,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":70.824,"r":501.94,"t":425.8617029101563},"charspan":[0,121],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"a) Applied voltage required to reach a luminance of 1 cd m -2 . b) Values at 1000, 5000 and 10000 cd m -2 , respectively."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"To elucidate the origin of the high performance of the Device 1, three reference devices (Devices 2, 3 and 4) with the same configuration as Device 1 were fabricated by using double neat films of FPPCA (20 nm)/Bepp2 (10 nm) and a single doping film of Bepp2:FPPCA (D) (1.5 wt%, 30 nm) and FPPCA (H):BZQPG (0.8 wt%, 30 nm) as the EML, respectively (see Figure S2 in ESI file). The efficiency-luminance (PE/EQEL ) characteristics of Devices 2, 3 and 4 and their EL spectra at different luminances (1000, 2500 and 5000 cd m  2 ) are shown in Figures  3c  and  4 .    The  two  emission  peaks  in  Device  2  are  assigned  to:  (i)  direct  exciton generation on the Bepp2 and FPPCA molecules in the respective EML and (ii) singlet/triplet excited state energy in the blue EML transferring to the green EML; these are similar to those of  Device  1  ( Figure  3b )  where  both  low-content  dopants  have  almost  no  effect  on  the inherent properties of the host of Bepp2 and FPPCA. Devices 3 and 4 comprise EMLs with","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":93.50398291015631,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":70.824,"r":527.5,"t":381.68598291015627},"charspan":[0,1020],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"To elucidate the origin of the high performance of the Device 1, three reference devices (Devices 2, 3 and 4) with the same configuration as Device 1 were fabricated by using double neat films of FPPCA (20 nm)/Bepp2 (10 nm) and a single doping film of Bepp2:FPPCA (D) (1.5 wt%, 30 nm) and FPPCA (H):BZQPG (0.8 wt%, 30 nm) as the EML, respectively (see Figure S2 in ESI file). The efficiency-luminance (PE/EQEL ) characteristics of Devices 2, 3 and 4 and their EL spectra at different luminances (1000, 2500 and 5000 cd m  2 ) are shown in Figures  3c  and  4 .    The  two  emission  peaks  in  Device  2  are  assigned  to:  (i)  direct  exciton generation on the Bepp2 and FPPCA molecules in the respective EML and (ii) singlet/triplet excited state energy in the blue EML transferring to the green EML; these are similar to those of  Device  1  ( Figure  3b )  where  both  low-content  dopants  have  almost  no  effect  on  the inherent properties of the host of Bepp2 and FPPCA. Devices 3 and 4 comprise EMLs with"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"9","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":36.2639829101563,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":294.67,"r":303.67,"t":46.595982910156295},"charspan":[0,1],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"9"}],"version":"1.10.0"}